title: "Causal Self: Constraint Computation, Causal Self-Models, and the Geometry of Inference"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Miliaresis
    given-names: Yiannis
repository-code: "https://github.com/pikos-apikos/causal-self"
url: "https://github.com/pikos-apikos/causal-self"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-05
abstract: >-
  A research hypothesis and experimental program asking whether structural
  causal self-models reduce inference cost under ambiguity. The program defines
  falsifiable sub-claims, discriminating controls, operational variables, and an
  artificial-agent protocol for testing self-indexed causal provenance.
keywords:
  - causal self-model
  - constraint computation
  - agency
  - provenance
  - metastability
  - inference geometry
